  witness cmd/BonfyreParticipation/tests/peer_facets_test.c checks distinct consent epochs, reciprocal choices, block, common interests and a 300-member invitation priority case
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/profile_site_scope.test.mjs checks the private connections tab against a fixture with no Participation owner: facet grammar, public refusal, sign-in redirect, same-origin mutation and the not-installed state
  invariant joining one context does not enroll a person in another context or in dating; leaving and rejoining invalidates choices and previously selected interests
  invariant optional interests are scoped to the current participation epoch and only their exact intersection is shown to two active members of the same context
  invariant candidate priority is decided across the eligible set before the bounded page is selected; blocks and passes remain excluded
  invariant private context messages require current reciprocal acceptance and preserve participation and choice revisions on every send and read
  forbidden_inference a private context message -> public speech, dating enrollment or a message in another context
  forbidden_inference shared interests -> consent to contact, friendship, physical proximity or a right to publish another person material
  forbidden_inference a public profile -> private participation or a dating eligibility witness
  known_gap the two-session browser acceptance (joins, interests, reciprocal acceptance through WebAddress) was not carried into main's profile fixture, which runs without a Participation owner; only peer_facets_test.c exercises the owner end to end
  known_gap interest tags are not event attendance, location or a semantic compatibility score; live deployment and migration are separate from local witnesses

interaction profile-connections-to-participation
  source account-peer-connections
  destination cmd-participation
  relation reads_and_writes_explicit_contexts
  preserves authenticated actor, context scope, participation revision, consent and blocks
  drops public disclosure of private choices or a claim of geographic proximity
  forbidden_inference a profile context -> independent authority over another person
